# Corpus unit bbox/C02 — gap (comparative; cost_accounting_comparison -> controlled_comparison)
#
# Source: bbox C02 annotation (comparative; corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: BBOX-ADAPTER
# full-step training costs $3.48 (StrategyQA) / $11.58 (GSM8K) vs Azure SFT $153.00 / $216.50, an
# ~31.30x mean cost reduction under one gpt-3.5-turbo-1106 pricing snapshot.
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Family map: cost_accounting_comparison -> controlled_comparison. Q = training_cost names the
#     compared quantity; the four dollar cells and the 31.30x mean-of-ratios aggregation live in
#     `nl` and refs (constants-only formal atoms).
#   * The annotation's own mandatory CQ3 is unmet-gap: the A100 adapter-training compute listed in
#     E03 Setup is never dollarized, so the total-cost premise is unestablished. Mapped onto the
#     nearest policy-mandatory CQ measurement_validity (the cost metric does not validly capture
#     total training cost). The incomplete controlled_comparison argument is declared as a
#     located hole with `open measurement_validity` (lowering re-done for issue #15 under
#     `lara-core@0.3`): it is not an AF node, so the claim lands `gap` on empty complete support.
#   * variance_reported (policy-mandatory) also has no discharging leaf: costs are single-snapshot
#     deterministic API billing with no repeats, so under the uniform standard it is undischarged
#     as well and is also opened. Either blocker forces gap; measurement_validity is the
#     annotation-grounded driver.
#   * CQ1 (same pricing/accounting) discharges baseline_parity; CQ2 (accuracy recorded, cost not
#     confounded by a quality drop) maps to the optional scope_match. Both leaves are on the page.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact bbox at sha256:bb06e592cef6
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------

claim c02
  nl      = "BBOX-ADAPTER full-step training costs $3.48 (StrategyQA) and $11.58 (GSM8K) vs Azure SFT $153.00 and $216.50, an approximately 31.30x mean cost reduction under one gpt-3.5-turbo-1106 pricing snapshot; A100 adapter compute is never dollarized"
  formal  = better(bbox_adapter, azure_sft, training_cost, strategyqa_gsm8k)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

leaf e1 : reports(e03, compares(bbox_adapter, azure_sft, training_cost, strategyqa_gsm8k, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C02, logic/experiments.md#E03, logic/experiments.md#E03-Procedure-step-5]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(bbox_adapter, azure_sft, e03)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03-Setup, logic/experiments.md#E03-Procedure-steps-1-5]

leaf e3 : scope_matched(bbox_adapter, training_cost, strategyqa_gsm8k)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03-Procedure-step-7, logic/experiments.md#E03-Metrics]

# --- ... and the incomplete argument is declared as a located hole ------------------------------

# valid_measurement(training_cost, e03) has no honest leaf (A100 adapter compute is never
# dollarized, CQ3) and variance_reported(e03) has none either (single-snapshot billing). Both are
# policy-mandatory and stay open: a1 is a hole, not an AF node.
arg a1 : supports(c02) by controlled_comparison(bbox_adapter, azure_sft, training_cost, strategyqa_gsm8k, e03)
  discharge baseline_parity      with e2
  discharge scope_match          with e3
  open      measurement_validity
  open      variance_reported

status c02

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: no arguments.
# Located hole: a1 (open obligations [measurement_validity, variance_reported]; sources no attacks).
# Claim status:
#   c02 -> gap (empty complete support; statusC = Gap iff null claimSupport, spec §8 — the hole
#               is reported, not a node)
